### Page 5 of 20

```text
PUDC-24-200

December 2, 2024
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to approve the 5th Street Towns Preliminary Plat, advancing the Final Plat to the Governing Body
with staff recommended conditions and acknowledgements.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

x
UDC 2.1.2 Preliminary Plat Approval
x
UDC 2.1.3 Final Plat Approval
x
UDC Article 4 Subdivisions
x
UDC Article 5 Zoning Regulations
x
PlanCheyenne

BACKGROUND:

The applicant is requesting approval of a preliminary plat for roughly 0.13 acres of land. The subject property
is vacant. The proposed plat would subdivide the parcel into four townhouse lots. These lots would meet the
requirements to be considered AD1 Lots, which are permitted in the MR Medium-density Residential zone.

Townhome (“attached”) lots are not allowed front access if the lot is less than 36’ wide. The plat does not
provide an access easement or alley for access to the central lots. The applicant is not intending to provide
driveways or garages with this development and will utilize on-street parking. Due to the frontage of the lots,
two full parking spaces cannot be provided adjacent to each individual lot. If the development is taken
collectively, the four lots proposed with available on-street parking would be able to provide at least 7
parking spaces, but the UDC only allows Staff to consider the area directly abutting each individual lot when
enforcing parking requirements. Should the Planning Commission and the Governing Body find the
development pattern acceptable and approve the plat with the understanding of the product proposed, an
administrative adjustment would be granted by Staff for reduced parking to one space per unit.

Although the plat as proposed meets all dimensional standards in the UDC for AD1 lot types, the specific
product desired by the applicant would require setback relief. Should the Planning Commission and the
Governing Body find the development pattern acceptable and approve the plat with the understanding of
the product proposed, an administrative adjustment would be granted by Staff for reduced rear setback. The
reduction would be to 10feet.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

Future Land Use Designation  Zoning
